-        "content": "# Model Non-Dependence Law V1\n\nStatus: CANONICAL / MANDATORY\n\n## Core law\n\nProject Brain, Astra, Superheroes, and Super-Workers MUST NOT depend on any language model, frontier model, or pretrained model as the system's brain, cognition source, or mandatory decision loop.\n\nA model is only an optional external knowledge/action source, comparable to:\n- web search\n- GitHub\n- documentation\n- databases\n- APIs\n- Wolfram and solvers\n- local files\n- browsers and computers\n- experiments and simulators\n- connected applications\n- humans when genuinely necessary\n\nModels may be used only when they are the best available source/tool for the specific missing knowledge, transformation, prediction, or action according to the system's objective function.\n\n## Mandatory cognitive architecture\n\nThe persistent cognitive loop is model-independent:\n\nGOAL\n\u2192 RECONCILE CURRENT STATE\n\u2192 IDENTIFY CAUSAL FRONTIER\n\u2192 DECOMPOSE\n\u2192 DETECT MISSING KNOWLEDGE / CAPABILITY / ACTION\n\u2192 DISCOVER EXISTING SOURCES AND TOOLS FIRST\n\u2192 SELECT BEST ROUTE BY CORRECTNESS, VERIFIED WALL-CLOCK, COST, AND EVIDENCE QUALITY\n\u2192 EXECUTE / EXPERIMENT / RETRIEVE\n\u2192 VERIFY\n\u2192 UPDATE PROJECT BRAIN\n\u2192 RECOMPUTE FRONTIER\n\u2192 CONTINUE\n\nNo step above requires an LLM.\n\n## Knowledge law\n\nKnowledge belongs in Project Brain and durable evidence stores, not inside model weights or a model context window.\n\nIf a fact, method, capability, or decision matters, it must be externally recoverable, attributable, and verifiable.\n\n## Tool/source selection law\n\nFor every knowledge or action need, the system MUST search and compare available routes before selecting one.\n\nExamples:\n- current factual knowledge \u2192 web/search/database/API\n- exact computation \u2192 Wolfram/code/solver\n- software capability \u2192 repositories/packages/APIs/tools\n- UI action \u2192 browser/computer\n- uncertain hypothesis \u2192 experiment/simulation\n- synthesis/reasoning where a model is fastest/best \u2192 model\n- model unavailable/rate-limited \u2192 continue through other routes\n\nA model is never privileged merely because it is called AI.\n\n## Search-before-invention law\n\nSearch existing tools, repositories, papers, APIs, services, social sources, datasets, and prior Project Brain work before inventing a new mechanism.\n\nInvent only after the relevant search space has been explored to the level justified by expected value and wall-clock cost.\n\n## Persistence law\n\nThe Superhero identity, mission, state, causal frontier, evidence, leases, verification status, and continuation loop MUST survive the loss of any model invocation or model provider.\n\nA model call can terminate; the Superhero must continue.\n\n## Runtime implication\n\nAny runtime that places a model call inside the mandatory supervisor loop is architecturally non-compliant and MUST be repaired.\n\nThe supervisor is responsible for:\n- mission persistence\n- state reconciliation\n- frontier computation\n- source/tool discovery\n- route selection\n- execution dispatch\n- evidence collection\n- verification\n- Brain update\n- continuation\n\nModels are registered only as optional providers in the source/tool registry.\n\n## Promotion rule\n\nNo runtime may be promoted as a real Superhero/Super-Worker if its continued cognition depends on one model, one model provider, or one model context remaining available.\n\n## Objective\n\nUse every available source of knowledge and capability, including models when they are actually best, to reach the verified goal in minimum wall-clock time at hard $0 incremental spend while preserving correctness, evidence, recoverability, and provider independence.\n",
+        "content": "# Model Non-Dependence Law V1\n\nStatus: SUPERSEDED / DO NOT EXECUTE\n\nSuperseded by:\n- `canonical/laws/MODEL_PROVIDER_RESILIENCE_AND_CAPABILITY_OWNERSHIP_LAW_V2.md`\n- `canonical/laws/FRONTIER_KNOWLEDGE_CAPABILITY_OWNERSHIP_MISSION_LOCK_V5.md`\n\nCritical correction: model-independence is not a terminal requirement. Models may participate in permanently configured Brain capabilities. The governing distinction is permanent capability ownership versus external/JIT knowledge, with an Opus-5.5-or-better useful-capability acceptance bar.\n",
         "path": "canonical/laws/MODEL_NON_DEPENDENCE_LAW_V1.md",
         "truncated": false,
         "type": "read_file"
@@ -56,7 +63,7 @@
